The 1998 Holli Dance by David White, the version that the SGI benchmark
table at www.sgidepot.co.uk/hollibench.html was measured with: run
"hollidance-1998", which prints the frame rate ("Frames Per Sec") on
standard output, to compare a machine with the table. For the current
version, see hollidance.

These are the author's IRIX binaries (n32; HolliDance5.3 is the o32 build
for IRIX 5.3, without audio). The NoStrobe file keeps the strobe light
effect off, because strobing light can cause seizures in people with
epilepsy; hollidance-1998 always keeps it in place.
